struggling with terrible poverty in 1970s Scotland, Doug decided a pit job would provide his wife and young family much needed security, despite extraordinary risks to life and limb. Every day, Cath kissed her husband goodbye, not knowing if she'd see him again as he went to work at the coalface, and while her husband toiled deep below, the mother-of-five put her cooking and cleaning skills to use in the colliery canteen. In good times and bad, the miner's wives pulled together as much as their men underground. Then Thatcher swept to power and suddenly loyalties were tested and a fight for survival of a different kind ensued. One for their very existence.\"--Back cover."},"isbn_10":["1471318125"],"covers":[10388754],"full_title":"At the coalface","key":"/books/OL29387353M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL8215967A","name":"Catherine Paton Black"}],"ocaid":"atcoalface0000blac","publish_places":["Bath"],"subject_times":["20th century"],"isbn_13":["9781471318122"],"pagination":"pages cm","source_records":["ia:atcoalface0000blac","ia:atcoalfacemylife0000blac_c9i0","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2020-07-30"],"title":"At the coalface","dewey_decimal_class":["331.4822334092"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Originally published: London: Headline, 2012."},"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"subject_places":["Great Britain","Scotland"],"subjects":["Coal miners' spouses","Working class women","Coal Strike, Great Britain, 1984-1985","Social conditions","Large type books","Working class","Biography"],"subject_people":["Catherine Paton Black"],"publish_country":"enk","publish_date":"2013","by_statement":"Catherine Paton Black","oclc_numbers":["816165315"],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL21470276W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"local_id":["urn:bwbsku:KN-831-420"],"identifiers":{"amazon":[""]},"latest_revision":3,"revision":3,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-08-25T08:19:32.547104"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-12-10T02:05:33.953663"}}},"O